== 5.7 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The modern periodic table arranges the elements in order of increasing],
  [atomic number],
  [valency],
  [relative atomic mass],
  [density]
)

#mcq(2, [A horizontal row of the periodic table is called a],
  [family],
  [group],
  [period],
  [block]
)

#mcq(3, [Elements in the same group have the same],
  [number of neutrons],
  [number of outer-shell electrons],
  [number of shells],
  [mass number]
)

#mcq(4, [The number of shells occupied by an atom is given by its],
  [atomic number],
  [mass number],
  [period number],
  [group number]
)

#mcq(5, [Elements in Group I are called],
  [alkaline earth metals],
  [noble gases],
  [alkali metals],
  [halogens]
)

#mcq(6, [Elements in Group VII are called],
  [alkali metals],
  [halogens],
  [noble gases],
  [transition metals]
)

#mcq(7, [The noble gases are placed in],
  [Group I],
  [Group VII],
  [Group II],
  [Group 0]
)

#mcq(8, [The noble gases are unreactive because],
  [they are all gases],
  [they are radioactive],
  [their outer shells are full],
  [they have no electrons]
)

#mcq(9, [Which of the following is the most reactive metal?],
  [sodium],
  [magnesium],
  [caesium],
  [potassium]
)

#mcq(10, [Reactivity in Group I increases down the group because],
  [the outer electron is further from the nucleus and more easily lost],
  [the atoms get smaller],
  [the number of protons falls],
  [the atoms gain electrons]
)

#mcq(11, [Which of the following is the most reactive halogen?],
  [fluorine],
  [iodine],
  [chlorine],
  [bromine]
)

#mcq(12, [Reactivity in Group VII decreases down the group because],
  [the atoms get smaller],
  [the atoms lose electrons],
  [the molecules become monatomic],
  [the incoming electron is less strongly attracted as the outer shell gets further out]
)

#mcq(13, [Chlorine displaces bromine from potassium bromide solution because chlorine is],
